SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Jokowi: Peace, Stability are Key to Global Economic Recovery","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-04-29","url":"https://setkab.go.id/en/president-jokowi-peace-stability-are-key-to-global-economic-recovery/","claim":"Jokowi said peace and stability are key to global recovery and that Indonesia's G20 presidency was pushing for a peaceful settlement of the Russia-Ukraine conflict.","locator":"lines 38-44","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidential-cabinet statement with dated remarks and direct attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period and tied to Jokowi's G20 diplomacy in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Jokowi as G20 chair and president; this is his public diplomatic posture, not an inherited baseline claim.","contrary_evidence":["It is a diplomatic statement, not proof of operational conflict restraint by itself."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"G20 president Indonesia seeks to ease crisis with Ukraine, Russia visits","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-06-23","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/06/23/g20-indonesia-russia-ukraine-int","claim":"Jokowi was to meet leaders of Ukraine and Russia to advocate peace and help ease the food crisis, and the trip was described as the first such visit by an Asian leader.","locator":"lines 601-605","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is strong independent corroboration, though carried through a syndication mirror.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Matches the lead-up to Jokowi's June 2022 Ukraine-Russia mission.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Jokowi's planned mission and foreign-policy choice as G20 chair.","contrary_evidence":["This is reporting about a planned mission, not the mission's complete results by itself."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Joint Press Statement of President of the Republic of Indonesia and President of Ukraine, at the Mariinsky Palace, Kyiv, Ukraine, June 29, 2022","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-06-29","url":"https://setkab.go.id/en/joint-press-statement-of-president-of-the-republic-of-indonesia-and-president-of-ukraine-at-the-mariinsky-palace-kyiv-ukraine-june-29-2022/","claim":"Jokowi emphasized respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity, said peace must be sought, offered to carry Zelenskyy's message to Putin, and pledged humanitarian assistance and support for hospital reconstruction and food-export security.","locator":"lines 39-45","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official transcript from the presidential secretariat with precise dated language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact target-period evidence for June 2022 international conduct.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Jokowi; this was his diplomatic action and public position.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is peace-oriented and does not show whether the effort changed battlefield conditions."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pernyataan Pers Bersama Presiden RI dan Presiden Rusia, di Moskow, Rusia, 30 Juni 2022","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-06-30","url":"https://setkab.go.id/pernyataan-pers-bersama-presiden-ri-dan-presiden-rusia-di-moskow-30-juni-2022/","claim":"Jokowi said peace and humanitarian issues were Indonesia's foreign-policy priority, that dialogue should remain open, that he was ready to be a bridge of communication, and that food and fertilizer supply chains needed urgent restoration with UN support.","locator":"lines 46-51","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official transcript of Jokowi's post-meeting remarks in Moscow.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 conduct during his Russia visit.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Jokowi and his stated mission to Putin.","contrary_evidence":["This is a self-described peace mission; it does not prove Russian agreement or concrete settlement terms."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.5","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Jokowi seeks to 'unite' G20 in talks with Ukraine, Russia","publisher":"The Jakarta Post","publication_date":"2022-04-29","url":"https://www.thejakartapost.com/world/2022/04/29/jokowi-seeks-to-unite-g20-in-talks-with-ukraine-russia","claim":"Jokowi refused Ukraine's request for military support and said Indonesia would send humanitarian assistance instead, while continuing support for peace negotiations.","locator":"final paragraph describing the refusal of military support and humanitarian alternative","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent national reporting on a specific ruler decision, consistent with official statements.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"In-period and directly relevant to Jokowi's response to a wartime request.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Jokowi as the decision-maker responding to Zelenskyy's request.","contrary_evidence":["The article is a report, not a verbatim official transcript of the refusal itself."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.5","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"United Nations Stands with People of Ukraine, Secretary-General Tells General Assembly, Stressing 'Enough Is Enough', Fighting Must Stop, as Emergency Session Gets Under Way","publisher":"UN Press","publication_date":"2022-03-01","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12404.doc.htm","claim":"Indonesia said the military attack on Ukraine was unacceptable, called for a peaceful resolution through dialogue and diplomacy, insisted on respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity, and urged safe passage for humanitarian aid and civilians.","locator":"Indonesia statement in the meeting coverage","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN meeting record captures the Indonesian delegate's statement contemporaneously and verbatim enough for attribution.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact March 2022 crisis response, before the Kyiv/Moscow mission.","ruler_attribution":"State-level foreign-policy posture attributable to Indonesia, with Jokowi as president and G20 chair.","contrary_evidence":["This is a diplomatic statement rather than direct command of military forces."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.6","2B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Aggression against Ukraine : resolution / adopted by the General Assembly","publisher":"UN Digital Library","publication_date":"2022-03-02","url":"https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/3959039","claim":"Indonesia voted in favor of the General Assembly resolution demanding Russia end its use of force and withdraw from Ukraine.","locator":"vote list showing INDONESIA as Y","source_type":"official/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN voting record is authoritative for the state vote and date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Early 2022 wartime response during Jokowi's term.","ruler_attribution":"State vote, not a personal speech, but still attributable to Jokowi's government at the UN.","contrary_evidence":["A yes vote is a state posture and does not by itself prove deeper operational peace leadership."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"General Assembly Adopts Text to Suspend Russian Federation from Human Rights Council, Continuing Emergency Special Session on Humanitarian Crisis in Ukraine","publisher":"UN Press","publication_date":"2022-04-07","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12414.doc.htm","claim":"Indonesia said it was deeply concerned about the humanitarian situation and Bucha reports, called for an independent investigation and objective, transparent procedures, and abstained from the vote.","locator":"Indonesia statement in the press release","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UN press coverage preserves both the reasoning and the vote outcome for Indonesia.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"In-period and directly relevant to Jokowi's response to the Ukraine crisis.","ruler_attribution":"State-level position; the abstention shows caution and process concerns under Jokowi's government.","contrary_evidence":["Abstention can be read as procedural caution rather than clear condemnation, so it is weaker than a yes vote."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.6","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indonesia dukung resolusi PBB mengutuk pencaplokan Ukraina oleh Rusia","publisher":"ANTARA News","publication_date":"2022-10-13","url":"https://www.antaranews.com/berita/3177773/indonesia-dukung-resolusi-pbb-mengutuk-pencaplokan-ukraina-oleh-rusia","claim":"Indonesia supported the UN resolution condemning Russia's annexation of Ukrainian regions and said the position followed respect for national integrity and international law.","locator":"opening paragraphs and quoted foreign-ministry explanation","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local-language reporting on Indonesia's UN stance, with direct foreign-ministry explanation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 escalation phase after annexation moves.","ruler_attribution":"State-level posture under Jokowi's presidency, with direct relevance to his foreign-policy line.","contrary_evidence":["This is a state vote and ministry explanation, not a direct presidential speech."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Remarks of President of the Republic of Indonesia During Third Session of G20 Summit on Digital Transformation, at The Apurva Kempinski Hotel, Badung Regency, Bali Province, November 16, 2022","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-11-16","url":"https://setkab.go.id/en/remarks-of-president-of-the-republic-of-indonesia-during-third-session-of-g20-summit-on-digital-transformation-at-the-apurva-kempinski-hotel-badung-regency-bali-province-november-16-2022/","claim":"Jokowi repeated that leaders must stop the war because war only hurts people and blocks global economic recovery.","locator":"opening remarks in session III","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official summit transcript with direct ruler attribution and clear date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact November 2022 summit conduct.","ruler_attribution":"Direct to Jokowi as G20 host and chair.","contrary_evidence":["This is summit rhetoric, but it is backed by the concrete diplomatic process and declaration below."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indonesian G20 Presidency Produces Bali Leaders' Declaration","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-11-16","url":"https://setkab.go.id/en/indonesian-g20-presidency-produces-bali-leaders-declaration/","claim":"Jokowi said the G20 leaders agreed to condemn the war in Ukraine because it violated borders and territorial integrity, and he framed the declaration as a major success of Indonesia's presidency.","locator":"lines 37-45","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidency transcript with direct attribution and clear policy content.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 summit-end evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal and institutional attribution to Jokowi as host of the summit.","contrary_evidence":["A G20 declaration is a multilateral outcome, not solely a personal achievement."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's war in Ukraine dominates G20 summit, with leaders agreeing to differ","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-11-15","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economic-indicators/g20-talks-enter-final-day-as-emergency-meeting-held-over-poland-blasts-2945221","claim":"Reuters reported that the G20 unanimously adopted a declaration condemning the war in Ukraine, that the declaration said the use or threat of nuclear weapons was inadmissible, and that Jokowi said the war had violated borders and integrity.","locator":"lines 416-427 and 429-431","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is strong independent corroboration of the summit outcome and Jokowi's remarks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact summit-period corroboration of the Indonesia-led G20 process.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to Jokowi as host; the declaration is multilateral but his summit leadership is clear.","contrary_evidence":["This is independently reported but still centered on a multilateral document, not a unilateral ruler act."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.7","2B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I considered roughly 30 documents across official Indonesian presidency/cabinet pages, UN meeting records and vote databases, Reuters syndication, ANTARA, The Jakarta Post, Detik, The National, and a few secondary roundup pieces.
- I kept the documents that added materially distinct claims: formal peace messaging, the Kyiv/Moscow mission, the refusal to arm Ukraine, UN votes, and the G20 declaration.
- I rejected duplicates that repeated the same core fact without adding a new claim or locator, especially multiple mirrors of the same Reuters story and multiple copies of the same official transcript.
- I rejected out-of-period follow-ups and retrospective summaries unless they were the only accessible source for a 2022 fact; those were not needed here.
- I rejected domestic governance, economic, or general Indonesia news items that did not materially bear on international peace, aggression, or lawful security.
- I also avoided padding with multiple publishers for the same event when the underlying claim was already covered by an official transcript plus one strong independent report.

**Remaining gaps**
- There is still no direct evidence of Indonesia taking or avoiding a coercive cross-border military action in 2022, which is unsurprising given the local prior showing no internationalized conflict events or fatalities.
- The strongest chapter-specific evidence is diplomatic and multilateral, not battlefield conduct. That means 2B.2, 2B.4, and 2B.5 are mostly informed by negative evidence and explicit restraint, not by combat command decisions.
- I found no material evidence that Jokowi manipulated intelligence or used military force for diversionary conflict in 2022.
- More search would probably yield only marginal nuance unless you want a tighter audit of Indonesia's UN voting explanations or additional corroboration of the Ukraine mission and G20 negotiation process.

I did not score.
